<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n112373" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φροντ-ιστής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οῦ</span>,
			ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>deep thinker,</i> as Socrates is called in derision by
				<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Nu.</u>
				266
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				414
			</span></i> (anap.), al.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φ. τῶν μετεώρων, τῶν
				οὐρανίων,</span>
			<i>one who meditates on</i> supra-terrestrial things, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Smp.</u>
				6.6
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Mem.</u>
				4.7.6
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ . . μετέωρα φ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Ap.</u>
					18b
				</span></i>
			: hence, generally, <i>philosopher,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Smp.</u>
				7.2
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>one who takes care of,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινων</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				37.8
			</span></i>; <i>curator,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱεροῦ Ἀφροδίτης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IGRom.</u>
					1.1167<i>C</i>4
				</span></i>
			 (Egypt, <span class="entity">ii A. D.</span>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">συναγωγῆς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>JHS</u>
					28.195
				</span></i>
			 (<span class="entity">Side</span>), cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>BMus.Inscr.</u>
				1069
			</span></i> (Fayum, <span class="entity">ii A.D.</span>); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν
				δημοσίων πραγμάτων</span> Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Pl.</u>
				908
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν ἀρχομένων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Poll.
					1.40
				</span></i>
			: <i>manager,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κακῷ φ. τὰ καθ᾽ ἑαυτοὺς ἐπιτρέψομεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Porph.
					<u>Abst.</u>
					1.50
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρύγρων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Cat.Cod.Astr.</u>
					8(1).177
				</span></i>
			; without gen., <i>manager, housekeeper,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Oec.</u>
				p.51
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				J.
			</span></i>: as transl. of Lat. <i>procurator,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ φ. Δρούσου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IGRom.</u>
					4.219
				</span></i>
			 (<span class="entity">Ilium</span>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> title of official of a <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φρατρία,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				14.759.8
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Naples</span>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>bailiff, house-steward,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Gp.
				7.8.1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>BGU</u>
				603.2
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii A. D.)</span>, etc.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
